Writes the document your brief names to the corpus. Code adds its kind, category, sub-category and scope from the topic, and checks the corpus contract all at once, naming every problem; the corpus file is written only once it all passes. Each section is a `##` heading and its text: the heading descriptive enough to make sense alone in a search result, the text self-contained, 1,000 to 2,000 characters. `knowledge_kind: implementation` needs `applies_to`, and `applies_to` needs `verified_on`.

Every try is kept, passing or not. The first call gives the whole document; after that, give only the sections that change: a section replaces the one with the same heading where it stood, a new heading is added at the end, and `drop` takes sections out by heading. Never send an unchanged section again. Each written version is kept as a record.
